    const steps=[
      `<p class="fine-print"><strong>Collateral destination · ${yn(v.verdicts.collateralToProtocolSmartWallet)}</strong> — ${v.collateralDestination==='protocol-smart-wallet'?'collateral is received at a smart wallet address the protocol controls — the collateral lives where programmable tokens live, under the protocol’s own control.':v.collateralDestination==='protocol-ordinary-address'?'collateral is received at an ordinary address the protocol controls — where programmable tokens never live, so the collateral the spec addresses to the protocol’s smart wallet is not there.':'collateral is received at the user’s smart wallet — an address the user controls, not the protocol, so the protocol has not received the collateral at an address it controls.'}</p>`,
      `<p class="fine-print"><strong>Deposit transfer logic · ${yn(v.verdicts.depositInvokesTransferLogic)}</strong> — ${v.verdicts.depositInvokesTransferLogic?'transferLogicScript validation applies when collateral is deposited, so the token’s transfer logic validates the deposit.':'transferLogicScript validation is skipped on deposit — collateral arrives without the token’s transfer logic ever validating the move.'}</p>`,
      `<p class="fine-print"><strong>Withdrawal transfer logic · ${yn(v.verdicts.withdrawalInvokesTransferLogic)}</strong> — ${v.verdicts.withdrawalInvokesTransferLogic?'transferLogicScript validation applies when collateral is withdrawn, so the token’s transfer logic validates the withdrawal.':'transferLogicScript validation is skipped on withdrawal — collateral leaves without the token’s transfer logic ever validating the move, however carefully deposits were validated.'}</p>`,
      `<p class="fine-print"><strong>Liquidation registry proofs · ${yn(v.verdicts.liquidationIncludesRegistryProofs)}</strong> — ${v.verdicts.liquidationIncludesRegistryProofs?'liquidation transactions include proper registry proofs, so each liquidated token’s registration — or non-registration — is proved in the liquidation itself.':'liquidation transactions omit registry proofs — the liquidation carries no proof of the tokens’ registration, and the spec requires proper registry proofs in exactly these transactions.'}</p>`,
      subLine,
    ].join('');
    return `<span class="mini-label">${head}</span>${summary}${steps}<p class="fine-print">Judged locally against the lending profile entered — the profile is the reviewer’s own reading of the protocol, entered here. PRISM inspected no lending protocol, read no registry, and no chain state, and built, signed, and submitted nothing: this checker judges whether the spec’s lending duties are claimed in the right places, never a protocol’s code.</p>`;
